---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE, DISCLAIMER } from '../config';
import { url } from '../lib/url';
---

<Base title="About" active="about" description={`About ${SITE.name}: who wrote it, why, and how to get in touch.`}>
  <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
  <h1>About this research</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <p class="lede">
      I built this to practise the work an early-stage investor does: finding companies before they are obvious, understanding the
      product and the people, and committing to a view with the reasoning on show.
    </p>
    <h2>Who</h2>
    <p>
      {SITE.author}.
      {SITE.linkedin && <span> <a href={SITE.linkedin} rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a>.</span>}
      {SITE.github && <span> <a href={SITE.github} rel="noopener">GitHub</a>.</span>}
      {SITE.contactEmail && <span> <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.</span>}
    </p>
    <h2>What this is</h2>
    <p>
      Independent desk research on pre-seed European companies with strong technology or product, written from the perspective of a venture
      investor in Europe or the US. The <a href={url('/methodology/')}>methodology</a> explains how companies are chosen and judged and the
      <a href={url('/scorecard/')}>scorecard</a> shows the weights. Everything is open to challenge.
    </p>
    <h2>For founders and companies</h2>
    <p>
      The theses are written from public information only. I have not spoken to the companies, seen their financials or visited their
      customers, and each page says so. If a fact is wrong or out of date, please tell me and I will fix it promptly. A company being
      listed here, or receiving a particular verdict, is a view on the evidence available to me, not a judgement on the people.
    </p>
    <h2>For investors and recruiters</h2>
    <p>
      The one-page summary on each deep dive prints cleanly to PDF. If you disagree with a weighting or a verdict, the sliders on the
      home page show how the ranking changes, and I am happy to talk through the reasoning.
    </p>
    {
      SITE.aiDisclosure && (
        <>
          <h2>How it was made</h2>
          <p>{SITE.aiDisclosure}</p>
        </>
      )
    }
    <h2>Limits</h2>
    <p>{DISCLAIMER}</p>
    <p><a href={url('/changelog/')}>See the changelog</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
